        "Ya-Sin"
      ],
      "explication": "This verse, known as the Verse of Light, describes the light of Allah guiding the believers.",
      "source": "Surah An-Nur (24), verse 35"
    },
    "316": {
      "question": "According to Surah Al-Kahf, what is better with Allah in reward?",
      "options": [
        "Power",
        "Fame",
        "Lasting good deeds",
        "Wealth and children"
      ],
      "explication": "Wealth and children are an adornment of this life, but lasting good deeds are better with Allah.",
      "source": "Surah Al-Kahf (18), verse 46"
    },
    "317": {
      "question": "How does Surah Al-Hadid describe the present life?",
      "options": [
        "A mere dream",
        "A play, an amusement and a deceptive enjoyment",
        "A happy eternity",
        "An endless exile"
      ],
      "explication": "Worldly life is described as a play, an amusement and a deceptive enjoyment compared with the Hereafter.",
      "source": "Surah Al-Hadid (57), verse 20"
    },
